  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 with multiprofile+avgpool (config_005, acc 0.650) is the strongest RNA-only result, and adding image (config_030, acc 0.632) actually underperforms it, confirming image is a weak/negative contributor. The scgpt encoder has not been tested in any experiment, leaving a critical gap in our understanding of which RNA representation is best. Question: Does scgpt outperform scvi_n200 as a single-cell RNA encoder under identical conditions (multiprofile, avgpool)? config_008 is directly comparable to config_005, isolating only the encoder variable. Why best next experiment: Under a limited budget, resolving which RNA encoder is superior is the highest-leverage decision because it determines the backbone for all future multimodal and aggregation experiments. A single-variable comparison against a known result (config_005) gives clean evidence without confounding, and the outcome will either reveal a new best encoder to exploit or confirm scvi_n200 as the ceiling, letting us redirect remaining budget toward aggregation/fusion refinements."
